Deep-link: web route `/tesla-charging-sessions` resolves to `.teslaChargingSessions`
through `AppRouteParser` (pathSegment `tesla-charging-sessions`), so the page is
reachable + deep-linkable on both the macOS/iPad detail column and the iPhone stack.

Data sources (web parity, ADR-004 — no networking in the view):
  useVehicles                      -> GET /vehicles
  useTeslaChargingSessions(vin?)   -> GET /tesla/charging/sessions{?vin}        (sessions + summary)
  useRefreshTeslaChargingSessions  -> POST /tesla/charging/sessions/refresh{?vin} (403 -> businessOnly chip)
  The view binds through TeslaChargingSessionsPageModel; the data-source protocol is the KMP-core seam.
  The header RangePicker maps to the TeslaChargingSessionsRange preset enum (web useRangeState default 'all');
  the window is applied client-side over charge_start_datetime to the chart/map/table ONLY — the summary stat
  cards read response.summary (range-independent), exactly as the web does.

SI discipline (ADR-005): sessions carry SI watt-hours (total_energy_added_wh), SI seconds
  (charge_duration_s) and ISO timestamps; peak power is the wire kilowatt field. The table
  Energy column forces kWh at the render boundary (web convertEnergyFromSI(_, 'kWh')); the
  Total-Energy stat formats in the user's unit via @Environment(\.tsUnits) + Units.formatEnergy
  (web useUnits().formatEnergy). Cost / rate are plain decimals through the localized currency
  formatter. Nothing non-SI is stored or computed.

